GEM-X motion adapter notices

The code under gem/ (with LICENSE, ATTRIBUTIONS.md and LICENSES/) is vendored unmodified
from NVlabs/GEM-X at commit 4aef1452e5df171deff4f293c08e643eb450981e. It is licensed under
Apache-2.0 (the LICENSE file in this directory), except the per-file notices ATTRIBUTIONS.md
lists: the adapted Hand processing modules and the source-camera restoration function carry
LicenseRef-OpenMDW-1.1 (LICENSES/LicenseRef-OpenMDW-1.1.txt), the diffusion and rotation
utilities carry their MIT and BSD-3-Clause notices. The adapter runs GEM-X's body video path
only (gem-infer motion-video with Contact/IK); the Hand, rendering and training code is
vendored with the package but never run.

The code under kimodo/ is the part of nv-tlabs/kimodo at commit
e1c219c99b4b94ba48be1fb6a1cbc64ecee4c954 that exports a SOMA BVH, vendored unmodified and
licensed under Apache-2.0 (kimodo-LICENSE): kimodo/exports/bvh.py, the skeleton code it
builds on (kimodo/skeleton, kimodo/geometry.py, kimodo/tools.py, kimodo/assets.py) and the
somaskel77 skeleton assets. The text-to-motion model, the viewer, the other skeletons and
kimodo/__init__.py are not vendored.

The weights are NVIDIA's: GEM-X Body Pose (body_s240000.ckpt), Native77 Body Motion
(motion_native77_e774_s292175.ckpt) and the original ViTPose (vitpose.pth) from
huggingface.co/nvidia/GEM-X, licensed under the NVIDIA Open Model License. The SOMA-X v0.3.3
geometry assets are from huggingface.co/nvidia/SOMA-X (Apache-2.0). The person detector is
the YOLOX-X COCO ONNX export of the Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX 0.1.1rc0 release (Apache-2.0);
the creator's own detector, OpenMMLab's yolox_x_8xb8-300e_humanart, is published only on
download.openmmlab.com, which the Model contract cannot address. The recipe's Model
documents address every file by its SHA-256 and size; the platform verifies the bytes when it
ingests them.

run.py and export_motion.py are Vonk Forge adapters. run.py runs upstream's
`python -m gem.inference motion-video --task body --postprocess`
on the one input video, with the creator's unmodified release configuration read from a
scratch directory of links to the mounted files (its yolox_humanart.onnx is the mounted
YOLOX-X), and writes motion.bvh and motion.npz into one deterministic zip.
export_motion.py hands GEM-X's SOMA rotations and Hips positions to Kimodo's own
motion_to_bvh with standard_tpose=True.

py-soma-x 0.3.3 is installed without its declared cholespy dependency: no SOMA code imports
it and PyPI has no Linux aarch64 wheel for it. ONNX Runtime is the CPU package; there is no
aarch64 onnxruntime-gpu wheel, and GEM-X runs its detector on the CPU by default.

